Changelog: 31-10-2026 15:07:26

Version 2.2.0.

Changelog: 31-10-2026 14:56:28

Added. PortableWindow follows the screen it is on (owner, 31-10-2026: moved from a TV to the Ally's own screen, the
portal kept the TV's sizes and ran off the Ally's screen). Moved to another screen (Win + Shift + an arrow, or
move_to()), the window remembers it for the suite (suite.ini, look/screen), and the suite's apps open on it from
then on while it is attached (start_screen(); otherwise Windows' main display). On a screen of another size the app
starts again there, sized for it: PowerShell waits for the app to end, then starts its own command line again
(restart_command(), RESTARTED set). Not while it is busy (can_restart(): the managers' busy flag; the portal's
download or install): it waits and says so (waiting_to_move()).

Changelog: 31-10-2026 14:36:22

Fixed. PortableWindow: the screen sizes a window, never its layout. With wrapped text in it (the portal's line
under the tiles) Qt took the layout's minimum height at the window's narrowest width, where the text needs more
lines, and made a full-screen window taller than its screen: the portal was 1920 x 1099 on a 1080p TV, its
bottom 19 px on the Ally's screen under it (owner, 31-10-2026). The layout now sets no size on the window
(SizeConstraint.SetNoConstraint).

Changelog: 31-10-2026 12:33:29

Version 2.1.1.

Changelog: 31-10-2026 00:13:44

Fixed. RoundedToolTip: a tooltip with no room below the cursor opens above it (left of it with no room to the
right), as Qt's own does, where it was pushed up over the cursor and the button under it; and clicks go
through a tooltip to the widget below. A click on a button low in the window only hid the tooltip and took
two or three tries (Nexus Release Tool, owner, 31-10-2026).

Changelog: 30-10-2026 23:24:23

Version 2.1.0.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 22:46:16

