Changelog: 30-10-2026 21:19:45

Added. chip.py, the chip's live values on a Windows handheld: the temperatures and the power draw moved from Windows
Portable Test's temps.py, unchanged, with the GPU's load (ADL's INFO_ACTIVITY_GFX), the CPU's load (CpuLoad,
Windows' GetSystemTimes) and parts() for a header (owner, 30-10-2026: the portal's). portable.py: which wallpaper
the suite shows (owner, 30-10-2026): a picture dropped in the suite's wallpapers folder (wallpaper_folder(),
wallpapers(), picture_problem(): PNG, JPEG or WebP, wider than high, at least 1280 x 720), kept in suite.ini
(wallpaper_picture(), set_wallpaper_picture()), the suite's own while none is chosen or it is gone; and its
transparency in % (wallpaper_veil(), shade(), PortableWindow.set_wallpaper_veil()), SHADE until one is set, so the
look stays as it was.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 19:43:49

Version 1.1.0.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 19:09:13

Fixed. xbox.py reads and writes the Xbox app's paths as Windows paths on any system (ntpath, PureWindowsPath): on Linux a
Windows path was one name without folders, so an app added was never found as listed (CI Nexus, pytest (core), on the
push of 30-10-2026). On Windows as before.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 18:17:38

Added. xbox.py, the Xbox app's library on Windows (owner, 30-10-2026: the Windows Portable Suite in the Xbox menu):
the apps added there with My Library's + are in the Xbox app's own JSON file,
LocalState\ThirdPartyLibraries\CustomLibraryManagement\CustomLibraryManagement.manifest in its package folder (as
the Xbox app 2611.1001.9.0 wrote it on the owner's Ally; the CustomLibraryManagement\ beside ThirdPartyLibraries\ stays
empty). add() writes an entry as the Xbox app writes one (gameCache, {guid}: id, title, installLocation,
executableName, imagePath, the dates), never twice, the file backed up (.bak) first and written with the Xbox app
closed (with_xbox_closed(), started again after); a file in another shape is never written (FormatError).

Changelog: 30-10-2026 17:55:08

Fixed. The play mode closes only the emulator's main windows (play.main_windows(): visible, top-level, without an
owner, not a tool window): Steam's overlay has windows in the game's process too, and a close sent to every window opened
it over the game (the owner's Ally, 30-10-2026, shadPS4 with Galaga). play.run() takes confirm (press_enter(): Enter in
the main window, ASK = 1 s after the close) for an emulator that asks before it quits: shadPS4's "Are you sure you want
to quit?", which it has no setting to skip, stayed on the screen.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 17:55:08

Added. power.text() says Plugged in while the device is on its charger (owner, 30-10-2026), its percentage on battery;
status_clock() comes before it: the header shows the battery last of its values.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 17:18:10

Fixed. A program an app starts on Windows never gets the controller reader's SDL variables (platform.outside_bundle(),
APP_VARIABLES: SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy, SDL_AUDIODRIVER, SDL_JOYSTICK_ALLOW_BACKGROUND_EVENTS, PYGAME_HIDE_SUPPORT_PROMPT),
from a release and from the checkout alike. Steam draws with SDL3: started with SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy it made its login
window without a window and never signed in, in Desktop and in Xbox mode (the owner's Ally, 30-10-2026: started so,
Logged Off; without them, signed in within 15 s). That, not the lower-case name of Steam's program (windows_steam(),
1.0.0), kept the game managers' Steam from signing in: every start that failed had the variables. An emulator that
draws with SDL, started without Steam, would have shown no game either.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 16:11:24

Version 1.0.0.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 14:49:38

Added. play.py, the game managers' play mode (owner, 30-10-2026: one way out of every game, "Hold View + Menu,
everywhere"): play.run() starts the emulator outside the app's bundle, watches the controller (core's PygameSource)
and, with View and Menu held together for two seconds (HOLD), sends WM_CLOSE to the emulator's windows and its
children's, as Alt+F4 does; one still running ten seconds (GRACE) later is ended. It ends with the emulator, with its
exit code. play.launcher(): what a game's Steam shortcut starts, the app's own program with --play in a release, its
run.ps1 in a hidden PowerShell window from the checkout; played() tells such a shortcut from one made before.
QUIT_HINT, the line the managers show when a game starts.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 14:49:38

Fixed. steam.write_shortcuts() takes the artwork of a shortcut it takes out under the number that shortcut has, also
when the change's own entry would number it otherwise (a shortcut another program started, such as one made before a
game manager's play mode).

Changelog: 30-10-2026 14:49:18

Fixed. On Windows, Steam's folder is its name as on the disk (windows_steam(), os.path.realpath): Steam's registry
key has it in lower case, and steam.exe started as c:\program files (x86)\steam\steam.exe never signed in, its
login window made off the screen and the client Logged Off for hours (the owner's Ally, 30-10-2026, in Steam's own
logs: every start by that name, the game managers' since 29-10-2026, against every start as C:\Program Files
(x86)\Steam\steam.exe, which signed in within 15 seconds). That, not -silent, kept Steam from signing in.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 14:49:18

