Changelog: 29-10-2026 11:35:27

Added. The buttons every portable window shares (owner, 29-10-2026: "Close" on B was not clear): B goes back (from a pane to its card, from a page to where it came from; on a card it does nothing), View (⧉) exits the app and Menu (☰) opens the information of the pane that shows.
PortableWindow.go_back() takes the focus from a pane back to its card, exit_app() closes (an app overrides it to ask
first while it is busy), Menu opens the shown pane's InfoPill (info_pill(), show_info()) and closes the popup again;
common_items() ends a legend with ☰ Info, B Back (while B can act) and ⧉ Exit app, and update_legend() is called on
every move of the focus, so the legend follows it. VIEW, MENU, INFO, BACK and EXIT are core's; a tap on the ⧉ entry
now acts (the legend knew View only by the name "View").

