folder: %LOCALAPPDATA%\windows-portable-suite\<app id>\<app id>.log for the Windows Portable Suite's apps. An app
that names none keeps ~/.local/share/<app id>/<app id>.log, as before.

Changelog: 26-10-2026 21:46:30

Added. platform: the Windows side, for the Windows Portable Suite. suite_data() and suite_config() give a suite's
folder (%LOCALAPPDATA% and %APPDATA% on Windows, the XDG folders elsewhere), start_menu() the Start-menu programs
folder, open_path() opens a file, folder or URL with its own program (os.startfile on Windows, xdg-open elsewhere),
launch_in_terminal() runs a PowerShell command in a window of its own on Windows (powershell_command(): the exit file
and the "Press Enter" pause as with bash), and make_shortcut() writes a Windows shortcut. PATH_BUDGET (240 of
Windows' 260 characters) is what a suite's paths stay within. data_home(), config_home(), bin_home() and xdg_open()
are unchanged on every system, and nothing changes on Linux.

