25-10-2026); robertotorino.github.io/nexus/ is now the Nexus page.

Changelog: 25-10-2026 00:51:24

Fixed. appinfo: SUITE_REPO_URL and SUITE_MANUAL_URL use the suite's new name, Nexus (RobertoTorino/nexus, renamed
25-10-2026). GitHub redirects the repository's old address, so update checks kept working; the wiki's old address
ended with the rename, so every app's wiki link works again from its first release on this core.

Changelog: 24-10-2026 23:19:01

Added. sound: unmute(), the sound of an application unmuted in Bazzite's sound settings (owner, 24-10-2026: an
Unmute button beside Bazzite's volume in the managers; shadPS4 was found muted there, and the owner had muted
nothing). WirePlumber keeps the remembered mute in memory and writes its file itself, so the file is never
written: the application's playing streams are unmuted through PipeWire's PulseAudio interface (pactl), and
without one a silent stream of two seconds is opened under its name (paplay), unmuted and closed, which
WirePlumber stores as it stores a change in the sound applet; the stored value is read back. Proved on the board:
muted to stored unmuted in about 2 s, nothing left running (wpctl set-mute hung on such a stream there, so pactl
it is). The muted message names the button. Tests: with a stream playing, without one, and the failures.

Changelog: 24-10-2026 20:46:27

Fixed. widgets: WrappedLabel, a word-wrapped label whose minimum height follows its width, and
hint_label(follow_height=True) for one. A wrapped QLabel tells its layout a minimum of one line whatever it wraps
to, so a window at its minimum height took the extra lines from the widget with the stretch below: RPCS3 Manager's
Settings tab, its Sound box squeezed unreadable under the three-line introduction on the board (owner,
24-10-2026). Opt-in, nothing else changes. Test: the minimum follows the width and the text.

Changelog: 24-10-2026 19:23:03

Added. sound: the volume the desktop remembers per application (owner, 24-10-2026: every manager shows it; found
on the board with RPCS3 muted in Bazzite's sound settings, a game playing without a sound). WirePlumber's
restore-stream module keeps a volume and a mute per application in ~/.local/state/wireplumber/stream-properties,
also once the application is closed; stream_sound(name) reads the line of an application's output stream, and
describe(app, sound) gives the words a manager's Settings tab shows beside the emulator's own volume (Muted, 0 %
or the percentage, in red when a game would play without a sound) and the advice (the sound applet while a game
plays). Read only. Moved here from RPCS3 Manager, which found it; PCSX2 Manager takes it the same day. Tests: the
file as the board writes it (a space in a name, another stream's line, broken JSON), the state folder, the words.

Changelog: 24-10-2026 07:20:00

Fixed. covers: the Covers dialog (the SteamGridDB key) wraps its text at a readable width; as one line it made the
dialog as wide as the screen (owner, 24-10-2026, from PCSX2 Manager). Its text names the app's button for Steam
through a new edit_key(button=...) argument, "Update Game Mode" as before unless the app says otherwise; PCSX2
Manager says Update Steam. Test: the button's name in the dialog's text.

Changelog: 24-10-2026 05:06:10

Added. applog: a log file per app (owner, 24-10-2026), ~/.local/share/<app id>/<app id>.log, one line per thing the
app says or does with the time (DD-MM-YYYY HH:MM:SS), and every uncaught error with its traceback; the file turns
over at 1 MB with three older kept, and goes to stderr when its folder cannot be made. setup(app_id) once at start,
logger(app_id) wherever the app logs, tail() for a Log tab. PCSX2 Manager uses it first; the other apps can follow.
Test: tests/test_applog.py.

Changelog: 23-10-2026 07:00:42

Fixed. widgets: a Pill that cannot be clicked (setEnabled(False)) shows its value and caption in the theme's muted
text color, as a disabled button does; before, it looked the same as one that can be clicked. The rule is on the
labels' own disabled state, as Qt ignores an ancestor's pseudo-state in a selector. No other app disables a pill, so
only USB HD Control's Update pill changes. Test: tests/test_widgets.py.

Changelog: 22-10-2026 21:10:49

Added. sensors: the board's live values from /proc and /sys without root (CPU load, clock and temperature, GPU load,
clock, power, voltage and temperature, the GPU governor's range, VRAM, RAM, VRM and NVMe temperatures, network,
disk and fans), moved here unchanged from System Overlay so that USB IPS3.5 reads the same. New with it:
interfaces() lists the network interfaces, and net() and read() (Sensors.interface) can measure one of them; each
interface keeps its own previous reading. Without one, as System Overlay asks, the network is all interfaces but
loopback, as before. Test: tests/test_sensors.py
(moved with it, and a test for one interface) on the fake board in tests/board.py.

Changelog: 22-10-2026 18:07:44

Added. covers: artwork from SteamGridDB for the games the managers put in Steam (owner, 22-10-2026), with one API key
of the user's own for the whole suite in ~/.config/bc250-bazzite-suite/steamgriddb-key (mode 0600; edit_key() asks
for it in a dialog). A game is looked up by its title, without ™, ® and the bracket tags of a file name: the exact
name, else the first found; of each kind asked for (the portrait, the wide picture, the banner, the logo) the still
picture with the highest score, leaving out those marked nsfw, humor or epilepsy. What is found is kept in the app's
covers folder under Steam's own names, with a .done marker, so a game is asked for once; art() fits the pictures to
steam.ART's sizes for an app to lay over its drawn ones. A refused key or no network stops the lookup with a
message; the key goes only to SteamGridDB's API and is in no message. Test: tests/test_covers.py, with SteamGridDB's
answers recorded.

Changelog: 20-10-2026 20:21:21

Added. widgets: Pill, a MetricBox that is a button (the accent edge under the mouse or the keyboard focus; a click,
Enter or Space emits clicked), moved from the portal so every app can use it; same_width() keeps a row of boxes or
pills as wide as the widest, also when a value changes. Tests: tests/test_widgets.py.

Changelog: 19-10-2026 23:41:01

Added. theme: the suite's theme, gunmetal (the default), silver or warm, one choice for every app in
~/.config/bc250-bazzite-suite/theme (theme_name(), save_theme_name()). apply_theme() puts its palette and style sheet
on the application (buttons and tabs with a sheen, thin borders, the accent on focus and selection); create_app()
calls it, with the app's own sheet after the theme's. ACCENT is the theme's accent, surface_style() and muted() give
an app the theme's surfaces and secondary text. Self-contained, so an app not on core carries a copy.

Added. widgets: StatusPill, MetricBox and AppHeader follow the theme: a pill or box is the theme's surface with its
state or color as a thick left edge, the text in the theme's color; MetricBox.set_colour() changes it. The room
inside stays as it was. The tooltip's border is the theme's accent.

Changelog: 19-10-2026 03:24:21

Added. upstream: publish() and read_all(), the updates outside the suite an app can install now (a newer
HelixSR, a newer PCSX2 nightly build), one file per app in ~/.local/share/bc250-bazzite-suite/upstream/, for the
portal's notice. Standard library only and self-contained, so an app not on core yet carries a copy
(tools/tests/test_instance_copies.py keeps them equal).

Changelog: 19-10-2026 03:05:03

Added. wifi: every Wi-Fi adapter on the board (USB or PCIe) and whether the running kernel has a driver and
firmware for it, read from /sys, modules.dep and modules.alias, this boot's kernel log and iw, with rfkill and the
connection's band, signal and speed (the network's name left out); report() says what it means as BC-250 Bazzite
Test's levels. Standard library only, so the system python3 runs it (python3 -m bc250_core.wifi). It only reads.

Changelog: 18-10-2026 22:28:23

Added. steam.shortcut_icon(): the icon file for a Steam shortcut, the PNG beside an app's WebP icon
(images/<app-id>-128.png), as Steam may not read WebP. steam_art.draw_icon_art() writes the logo over the banner as
PNG when the icon is not one, since Steam's grid files are PNG.

Changelog: 16-10-2026 04:52:58

Added. steam_art.draw_icon_art(): the four pictures of a Steam shortcut drawn from an app's icon, for apps with no
pictures of their own. The background is near black in the icon's own color (the mean of its bright, saturated
pixels), lighter towards the middle, with a glow of that color; the portrait and the wide picture have the icon, a
title and a line under it, the banner the title and its own line centered, and the icon file itself is the logo. A
long title wraps and shrinks to fit. Without the icon the background is dark blue and the title is the logo. Moved
from Console Link, which drew it first; Console Link, the PCSX2 Manager and Bazzite DatStation use it. Tests: Steam's
sizes, the icon as the logo, the color taken from the icon, a long title and no icon.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 22:35:35

steam.write_shortcuts: a shortcut that is renamed gets a new Steam number (from its program and name), so the
artwork under its old number is removed, for every Steam user, unless another shortcut in the same change takes that
number. Before, it stayed behind in grid/. The emulator managers rename their shortcuts to "[PS4] Title" and the like.

